</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Qualitative Results</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Appendix E Qualitative Results ‣ Cross-Modal Content Optimization for Steering Web Agent Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> illustrates a query-only, black-box attack in which a human-imperceptible PGD perturbation causes a vision–language model to reinterpret the same image, evidencing sensitivity to small input-space changes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix E Qualitative Results ‣ Cross-Modal Content Optimization for Steering Web Agent Preferences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents a complementary text-side study: iteratively editing the movie description steers the web agent’s selection policy toward the desired target, yielding a markedly higher selection rate across successive revisions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
